// ============================================================
// SOLUTION 2: Load a Specific Old Version in MakeCode
// ============================================================
// Problem:
//   Pasting  https://github.com/org/repo#v0.6.3  in MakeCode Import URL gives:
//   "No such repository or branch" error.
//   Error in console: GET .../git/commits/undefined 404
//
// Root Cause:
//   MakeCode cannot resolve annotated git tags to a commit SHA.
//   It only handles branches reliably, not tags.
//
// Fix — Create a branch from the tag on GitHub.com (no git commands needed):
//   Step 1: Go to repo on GitHub → Tags → click the tag you want (e.g. v0.6.3)
//   Step 2: Click the branch pill (🏷 v0.6.3 ▾) near top-left of file list
//   Step 3: Switch to "Branches" tab in the dropdown
//   Step 4: Type new branch name, e.g.:  stable-v0-6-3
//   Step 5: Click "Create branch: stable-v0-6-3 from tag 'v0.6.3'"
//
// Then in MakeCode Import URL paste:
//   https://github.com/org/repo#stable-v0-6-3
//
// Rule: Always use a branch (not a tag) in MakeCode URLs. Tags don't work.


