// ============================================================
// SOLUTION 4: Fix Local Repo After Remote Default Branch Changed
// ============================================================
// Problem:
//   VSCode sync fails after changing default branch on GitHub:
//   "fatal: couldn't find remote ref master"
//   "[warning] No such branch: master"
//
// Root Cause:
//   Local repo is still tracking origin/master which no longer exists (or was renamed).
//
// Fix (one command):
//   git fetch origin
//   git checkout main--stable-v0-6-3
//
//   → Git auto-sets up tracking: "branch set up to track origin/main--stable-v0-6-3"
//   → VSCode sync now works correctly against the new default branch.


// ============================================================
// SOLUTION 5: MakeCode Loads Stale/Wrong Project When Signed In
// ============================================================
// Problem:
//   After importing a GitHub URL in MakeCode (signed in), MakeCode shows:
//   - TypeScript errors for names that exist in source files
//   - Wrong pxt.json content (e.g. old dependency URLs auto-modified by MakeCode)
//   - Hard browser reset (Ctrl+Shift+R) does NOT fix it
//   - Loading same URL in incognito (not signed in) works correctly ← KEY DIAGNOSTIC
//
// Root Cause:
//   MakeCode (signed in) saves a copy of every imported project to the user's
//   cloud account on MakeCode's servers. On re-import of the same URL, it loads
//   the CACHED cloud copy instead of fetching fresh from GitHub.
//   Confirmed by this line in the browser console log:
//     GET /api/user/project/411b26ed-c75e-4e9d-92f8-ba80fe475332  ← cloud copy, not GitHub
//
//   Hard browser reset only clears LOCAL browser cache — it does NOT clear
//   MakeCode's server-side project cache tied to the user account.
//
// Fix — Delete the stale cached project from MakeCode's home screen:
//   Step 1: Go to https://makecode.microbit.org/ (signed in)
//   Step 2: On the home screen, find the project in "My Projects"
//   Step 3: Click the three dots (⋯) on the project card → Delete
//   Step 4: Do a fresh Import → Import URL with the GitHub URL
//
// Result: MakeCode fetches clean from GitHub, no stale cache interference.
//
// Rule: If MakeCode behaves differently signed-in vs incognito → delete the
//       cached project from My Projects and re-import fresh.


// ============================================================
// SOLUTION 6: Duplicate Extension After MakeCode "Pull Changes"
// ============================================================
// Problem:
//   After updating pxt.json on GitHub (e.g. changing extension dependency URL)
//   and doing "Pull changes" in MakeCode, BOTH the old and new extension appear:
//   - Left panel shows both extensions, each with red error badges (100+ errors)
//   - Errors are all "Duplicate identifier" — same namespaces loaded twice
//   - pxt.json in MakeCode editor shows both old and new dependency lines
//   - Trash icon on old extension is disabled / greyed out — cannot delete
//   - Editing pxt.json directly in MakeCode editor to remove old line doesn't work
//     (MakeCode re-adds it stubbornly from its cached state)
//
// Root Cause:
//   MakeCode "Pull changes" MERGES GitHub's updated pxt.json with its own
//   cached project state (which still has the old extension). Both entries
//   end up in pxt.json and both extensions are loaded → duplicate identifiers.
//
// Fix — "Revert all" in MakeCode's GitHub sync dialog:
//   Step 1: Click the branch indicator button at the bottom of MakeCode screen
//           (shows "#main--stable-v0-6-3 ↑" or similar)
//   Step 2: In the dialog that opens, click "Revert all changes"
//   Step 3: MakeCode discards its merged/cached state and restores from GitHub
//   Result: Clean single-entry pxt.json, no duplicate extension, no errors
//
// Alternative Fix (if Revert all not available):
//   Delete project from My Projects → fresh Import URL (see Solution 5)
//   Use:  https://github.com/org/repo#branch-name
//
// Rule: After updating pxt.json on GitHub, always use "Revert all" in MakeCode
//       rather than "Pull changes" to avoid merge residue.
//
// Note: pxt.json dependency key (left side) is just a label — safe to rename.
//       pxt.json dependency value (right side) is the actual GitHub URL — this matters.


